.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
show program's version number and exit

.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
be verbose

.TP
\fB\-\-log\-level\fR \fI\,[<logger>=]<level>\/\fR
set the log level of a logger, e.g. interfaces.aardvark=DEBUG (can be repeated)

.TP
\fB\-J\fR, \fB\-\-json\fR
print the output as JSON (if supported)

.TP
\fB\-I\fR \fI\,<interface>\/\fR
interface (rmcp, rmcpplus, aardvark, ipmitool, ipmbdev, ipmidev, openipmblink)

.TP
\fB\-o\fR \fI\,<options>\/\fR
interface specific options (name=value, separated by commas, see below)

.TP
\fB\-t\fR \fI\,<addr>\/\fR
target IPMB address

.TP
\fB\-b\fR \fI\,<channel>\/\fR
target channel

.TP
\fB\-r\fR \fI\,<routing>\/\fR
target routing

.TP
\fB\-H\fR \fI\,<host>\/\fR
RMCP host

.TP
\fB\-p\fR \fI\,<port>\/\fR
RMCP port (default 623)

.TP
\fB\-U\fR \fI\,<user>\/\fR
RMCP user

.TP
\fB\-P\fR \fI\,<password>\/\fR
RMCP password

.TP
\fB\-L\fR \fI\,<level>\/\fR
RMCP privilege level (user, operator, administrator)

.SH COMMENTS
interface options (\-o name=value,...):
  aardvark:
    serial=<SN>        serial number of the device
    pullups=<on|off>   enable/disable pullups
    power=<on|off>     enable/disable target power
    fastmode=<on|off>  enable/disable 400kHz I2C bitrate (default 100kHz)
  ipmitool:
    interface_type     interface type to be used (lan, lanplus, serial, open)
    cipher             cipher to be used (0\-255)
    retries=<n>        number of retries for lan/lanplus (ipmitool \-R)
    timeout=<sec>      timeout of each try for lan/lanplus (ipmitool \-N)
  ipmbdev:
    port=<path>        path to Linux IPMB device (default /dev/ipmb\-0)
  ipmidev:
    port=<path>        path to Linux IPMI device (default /dev/ipmi0)
    timeout=<sec>      response timeout in seconds (default 10)
  openipmblink:
    port=<path>        data serial port of the bridge (default /dev/ttyACM1)
                       or pyserial URL of a shared bridge
                       (e.g. socket://localhost:5555)
    bus=<n>            IPMB bus of the bridge (default 0)
    address=<addr>     own IPMB address (default 0x20)
  rmcpplus:
    cipher=<id>        cipher suite (1, 2, 3, 15, 16, 17; default: try 17,
                       then 3)
    kg=<hex>           BMC key K_G as hex string (default: user password)

loggers (\-\-log\-level <logger>=<level>):
  interfaces.aardvark, interfaces.base, interfaces.ipmb, interfaces.ipmbdev,
  interfaces.ipmidev, interfaces.ipmitool, interfaces.openipmblink,
  interfaces.rmcp, interfaces.rmcpplus, interfaces.router
  A parent name sets all its children, e.g. 'interfaces', and without a
  name the level applies to all loggers.
.SH EXAMPLES
Print the device ID of a BMC over RMCP+ (IPMI v2.0, like \fBipmitool \-I lanplus\fR):
.PP
.RS
pyipmi \-I rmcpplus \-H 10.0.0.1 \-U admin \-P admin bmc info
.RE
.PP
List the sensors of a BMC over RMCP (IPMI v1.5):
.PP
.RS
pyipmi \-I rmcp \-H 10.0.0.1 \-U admin \-P admin sdr list
.RE
.PP
Print the FRU of the local BMC using the Linux IPMI driver:
.PP
.RS
pyipmi \-I ipmidev fru print
.RE
